  "name": "Alphabet cut-up (glitch spelling-bee)",
  "desc": "A frantic, stuttering cousin of the alphabet poem: each letter is chopped in two and machine-gunned, spliced with spoken numbers and gated by <> call-and-response masks so fragments drop in and out. degradeBy thins the stream generatively and every-rev spits phrases backwards. Short slap delays and perlin panning make it a glitchy, disoriented spelling-bee \u2014 abstract but locked to a pulse.",
